<section class="section"><div class="container story-block__grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Learn by doing</p><h2>Real understanding grows through use.</h2><p>Projects make learning visible. They help participants connect concepts, make decisions, solve problems and communicate what they have made. In organizational work, the equivalent is a functioning asset, an improved workflow or a team that understands how to sustain the change.</p></div><div class="principles-list"><div><span>01</span><p><strong>Begin with context.</strong> Understand people, constraints and the real problem.</p></div><div><span>02</span><p><strong>Make progress visible.</strong> Use reviewable stages and useful outputs.</p></div><div><span>03</span><p><strong>Build capability.</strong> Explain decisions and support responsible ownership.</p></div></div></div></section>
